<section | Inline-semantic and HTML-native inline elements>

The <abbr title="Document Object Model" | DOM> is the browser API for HTML.
An <term #term:eigenvector | eigenvector> is a non-zero vector that scales
under a linear transformation.

Press <kbd | Ctrl+C> to copy. The function takes a parameter <var | n>;
the command prints <samp | Hello, world!> to stdout; the function returns
<output | 42> for the test input.

Note: this fixture places `affiliation`, `orcid`, and `email` inside
`<meta>` as a convenient long-form-capable apparatus context — the
canonical structural home for those three is inside an `<author>` element
when authoring uses structured-author children, which is a separate
follow-on (the `<author>` long-form registration is not in this slice's
scope). The point of doc-26 is to prove the eleven new vocabulary
entries render correctly, not to lock in their final structural homes.
